# CLEAN BOOT of a 4 MB game with a long name (Hello.gba padded), the cart's
# ROM copy taking 128 frames (OMEGA_COPY_RATE, 32 KB a frame): the loading
# card shows the game's name and "Loading the game", and during the copy a
# VBlank interrupt moves the bar on the kernel's estimate (64 frames at
# PROGRESS_COPY_RATE, source/progress.h), a frame at a time, fast to 90% of
# the copy's share, then slower, never past its end. It draws in VBlank:
# no tears. The launch goes through the menu's test hook (tests/nav.sh).
#! sd-file "/Big Adventure - The Longest Subtitle (Europe) (En,Fr,De).gba" 0x400000 tests/roms/hello/hello.gba
#! env OMEGA_COPY_RATE=0x8000
-w "nav: home ready"
-P "@8:nav_test_path:/Big Adventure - The Longest Subtitle (Europe) (En,Fr,De).gba" -p @8:nav_test_action:0x7E000001
-w ", CLEAN BOOT"
-H @6:@12
-T @1:@130
-s @40:fast.png
-s @110:slow.png
-w "launch: the cart copied"
-s @0:copied.png
